    ('weapon_imbue_exclusivity', 'Weapon-imbue-type ability cards (Windfury Weapon, Flametongue Weapon, Fel Infused Weapon, Rockbiter Weapon, Frostbrand Weapon) share a weapon-enchant slot - only one active at a time. This is a mechanical slot conflict, separate from the talent all-damage% exclusivity bucket, and is NOT stated in any single tooltip - ask "is this an imbue?" before recommending one alongside another.', 'Primer', '§2 (v7)'),
    ('method_prefer_named_effect_talents', 'When hunting multipliers for a specific effect (e.g. Shadowflame damage), prefer talents that name the effect verbatim in their tooltip (Shadow and Flame, Bane both list "Shadowflame" explicitly) over talents matched by generic school wording (Emberstorm: "Fire and Shadow spells", does not name Shadowflame - a prediction under the hybrid double-dip rule, not a confirmed hit). Named lists are ground truth; generic wording needs a proc-test.', 'Primer', '§5 (v7)'),
    ('method_rank_id_decoding', 'When decoding a live in-game spell ID export (WeakAura, inspect addon) against the catalog, an unresolved ID is very likely a different rank of a known card, not missing content. Multi-rank talents appear to get a distinct spellID per rank in-game while the catalog stores one canonical ID per card. Check +/-1-3 of the unresolved ID for a known card name before concluding absence. Resolved 5/5 unmatched IDs this way in one live cross-check (Flurry, Vengeance, Fanaticism, Spellblade, Mental Quickness), each landing exactly on a card already known to be held at partial rank.', 'Primer', '§5 (v8)'),
    ('paladin_v6_loadout_confirmed', 'Live inspect/WeakAura export (55 spell IDs) cross-referenced against catalog for Paladin build, 2026-08-02. 22 of 25 v5 board talents confirmed unchanged. Shadow Strikes, Enhanced Weapon Mastery, and Seals of the Pure confirmed rerolled away since v5, replaced by Accuracy, Glyph of Seal of Command (deliberate temporary mana fix pending Spellblade 3/3), and Glyph of Blood Strike (unevaluated filler). Lunar Guidance independently confirmed slotted, matching the v5 hypothesis for the residual Duality SP gap. Berserker Stance, Ghost Wolf, Frostfall confirmed present but player-rated as low-priority leftovers, not core rotation.', 'Handoff', '§7/§12 (v6)'),
    ('goak_avenging_wrath_retraction', 'RETRACTED (v7): "Avenging Wrath / Guardian of Ancient Kings are substitutes, take the first" was wrong. They are independent cooldowns on separate systems - Guardian of Ancient Kings resets/discounts Hammer of the Righteous, Divine Storm, and Holy Shock cooldowns plus a Holy damage buff; Avenging Wrath is a flat all-damage/healing cooldown on its own timer. Both tooltips carry a "does not stack with other similar effects" clause, but that governs multiple instances of the SAME buff type, not necessarily exclusivity between these two specifically - and even under a worst-case mutual-exclusivity reading, sequential use on two separate cooldowns still nets more total burst-window uptime than picking only one. Both moved to the Paladin handoff chase list.', 'Handoff', '§8/§12 (v7)'),
    ('cross_character_ewm_observation', 'Cross-character observation (not a measurement, treat as evidence): Enhanced Weapon Mastery confirmed live (undisputed) on another player\'s comparable Paladin/Hammerdin spec, since his board carries none of the all-damage% exclusivity bucket\'s other members (no Answered Prayers, Unending Fury, Blessed Weapons, Blood Gorged, Improved Blood Presence). Same card is dead on our own build (bucket-blocked by Answered Prayers). Illustrates that a card\'s dead/alive status depends on full board composition, not the card in isolation.', 'Handoff', '§12 (v7)'),
    ('divine_storm_execution_sentence_sighting', 'Cross-character observation (not a measurement): another player\'s comparable Paladin/Hammerdin spec runs both Divine Storm and Execution Sentence live - both are on our own ability chase list (§8). Evidence they are obtainable and playable; not a substitute for our own parse data once acquired.', 'Handoff', '§8 (v7)'),
    ('doomhammers_fury_does_not_touch_molten_earth', 'Doomhammer\'s Fury (271580, granted by the Casting-Lava-Lash talent 271596) does NOT buff Lava Lash or Molten Earth. Raw DBC description (271580): "Your Pyroblast and Lava Burst now restore mana, generate a stack of Maelstrom Weapon, and deal $s1% increased direct damage" (EffectBasePoints[0]=12 -> s1=13%; EffectAura=[Dummy,ProcTriggerSpell,ProcTriggerSpell] triggering 271589 and 271587 for the mana-restore/Maelstrom-Weapon-stack grants). Confirmed NOT an amplifier for either Lava Lash or its Molten Earth spawn - third instance of the class-tag trigger-vs-modifier trap (primer §4 proof case #2 pattern: granted-by-X does not imply buffs-X). CONFIRMED via 2026-08-03 DBC pull (Titanus/Zavulon armory scouting session, report 74).', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('fel_infused_weapon_flat_and_2h_coefficients', 'Fel Infused Weapon (276076) tooltip formula ${$276075ppl1+$276075m1+$AP*0.05+$SP*0.05}: the AP*0.05/SP*0.05 terms were already in spell_scaling (source=export_tooltip). Raw DBC for hidden sub-spell 276075 ("Fel Infused Attack", school_mask=36 = Shadow+Fire hybrid): EffectBasePoints[0]=3, EffectDieSides[0]=3, EffectRealPointsPerLevel[0]=1.5 -> $276075m1 (min roll, basepoints+1) = 4, $276075M1 (max roll) = 6, $276075ppl1 = 1.5. Flat component ~5.5 (before AP/SP terms) at effective scaling level. Separately, 276082 ("Fel Infused Flames 2H damage increase", a % damage-done aura) has EffectBasePoints[0]=14 -> $276082s1 = 15% more Shadowflame damage while a single two-handed weapon is equipped. CONFIRMED via 2026-08-03 DBC pull (Titanus/Zavulon armory scouting session, report 74).', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('fire_strike_not_part_of_fel_infused_weapon', 'Searched the FULL client Spell.dbc (209,080 records, not just the 3,061-entry spell-export.json catalog) for every spell named "Fire Strike" - 50 name matches total, none scoped near 276075/276076/276082 and none appear in either spell\'s own EffectTriggerSpell array ([0,0,0] on both). Structurally, "Fire Strike" is NOT a second effect slot on Fel Infused Weapon\'s spell entry, nor a documented trigger of it. Fel Infused Attack (276075) is itself already a hybrid Shadow+Fire spell (school_mask=36); the client\'s combat log has no DBC-level mechanism to split one hybrid-school hit into two separately-named rows. The most structurally plausible unrelated candidate is the "lance of fire" item-proc family (spell IDs 313765/317765/321765, triggered by 313764/317764/321764 - "melee attacks have a chance to unleash a lance of fire... SP*0.16+AP*0.1 Fire damage", no ICD stated, pure Fire school), which would produce a coincidentally similar hit-count profile from a SEPARATE item/enchant rather than from Fel Infused Weapon itself. UNRESOLVED which exact "Fire Strike" ID logged for Zavulon without the actual spell ID from the raw combat-log API (name search alone is ambiguous across 50 candidates) - do NOT sum the Fire Strike row into Fel Infused Weapon\'s "~30% of total DPS" figure on this evidence; treat as a separate proc pending spell-ID confirmation from the log data. CONFIRMED-NEGATIVE via 2026-08-03 DBC pull (Titanus/Zavulon armory scouting session, report 74).', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('righteous_vengeance_zero_crit_reinforced', 'Righteous Vengeance 0% crit reinforced far beyond the original sample: 303 total hits, 0 crits, across 9 different characters (Titanus, Zyzz, Blix, Professorpp, Zavulon, Lootgoblin, Wynta, Xyz, Bigolecrits) spanning 4 different Paths (Duality, Strength, Intelligence, Agility). Path-independence makes this essentially settled, not just "still holding." SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, report 74 (Hakkar).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('molten_earth_crit_varies_by_character', 'Molten Earth crit rate is NOT a fixed/flagged value - it varies by character: 40.7% (575 hits, original primer v6/v7 sample), 46.6% (54/116, Zavulon/Duality), 64.8% (35/54, Titanus/Intelligence). Three independent measurements spanning a 24-point range. This REFINES (does not contradict) the existing "no structural predictor, per-spell server flag, verify per-parse" verdict - the more precise read is that Molten Earth is a normal crit-capable spell that scales with each character\'s own spell crit rating, same as any other spell, rather than having some fixed or capped crit value. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, report 74.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('holy_unresistable_means_no_full_resist', 'REFINEMENT to the existing "Holy is unresistable" combat-engine default (primer §1): confirmed via avoidance data that this specifically means no FULL resist roll, not immunity to partial/chip magic resistance. Lightbound Cleave (Holystrike, our own build): 356 hits across 3 targets, 0 miss/dodge/parry/resist_full, but nonzero partial resist (133/25/1 per target - damage reduced by a %, not avoided). Hammer from the Heavens (Holystrike, our own build, 11 characters pooled): 4,962 hits, 0 miss/dodge/parry/resist_full, 698 partial resists. Practical consequence: "unresistable" does not mean "ignore target resistance stat entirely" for damage forecasting, only "cannot be fully negated by a resist roll." SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, reports 59-86 (17 reports scanned).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('hammer_from_heavens_cannot_be_avoided', 'CONFIRMED, closes build_paladin-hammerdin.md open question (hit/expertise walkback §): Hammer from the Heavens cannot miss, be dodged, or be parried. 4,962 total landed hits pooled across 11 characters (Professorpp 2471, Geniusdex 988, Phantomx 774, Germarona 239, Linny 73, Xoller 49, Zenji, Chewy, Skipper, Scytrix, Givemegood) and 17 reports (ids 59-86): 0 miss_count, 0 dodge_count, 0 parry_count, 0 resist_full_count across the entire pool. Only partial/chip resist is nonzero (698 total) - see holy_unresistable_means_no_full_resist. This is a hit-table/avoidance-type finding, not a crit-table finding - crit table for Hammer from the Heavens was already separately confirmed via Holystrike (primer §1 v4). SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, character_damage_taken_abilities endpoint with participantType=enemies.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('titanic_mutilate_first_crit_data', 'Titanic Mutilate (external sighting, borrows Mutilate modifiers per class-tag rule, Physical school) has its first real crit data: main-hand 47.8% (11/23), off-hand 39.1% (9/23), on Zavulon/Duality. Consistent with melee-table crit given Physical school - not yet cross-checked against that character\'s own melee/spell crit sheet split, so treat as suggestive not confirmed-table. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, report 74.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_killing_machine_correlation_v2', 'Second independent sample supporting (not yet confirming) Killing Machine as the driver of Winds of Winter\'s near-100% crit rate: Titanus logged 12 Winds of Winter casts (15 hits, 15 crits = 100%) against 11 Killing Machine applications (55.8% average uptime) in the same fight - close to 1:1, consistent with a hold-for-proc playstyle. Does not fully prove the mechanism (would need cast-timestamp-vs-buff-interval overlap, which this API does not expose at that granularity). Existing primer/synergy doc open question stands, now with a second corroborating N. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 scouting session, report 74, buff_uptimes endpoint.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('combat_log_parser_field_layout_fix', 'combat_log_parser.py verified and fixed against a real 2026-08-03 Ascension log (Pumprat, Uldaman). Two bugs found: (1) this Ascension client omits sourceRaidFlags/destRaidFlags entirely - 6 base fields not the stock-WotLK 8, which had silently shifted spellId/amount/critical etc. by 2 columns and produced garbage tiny "spellIds" (223, 220...) with a flatlined 0% crit everywhere. (2) miss-type events are SPELL_MISSED/SWING_MISSED in this log, not SPELL_MISS/SWING_MISS - the old checks never matched, so avoidance_breakdown silently returned nothing for spell misses. Also decode_alc.py: the chunk-reassembly regex was capturing the CSV field\'s closing quote as part of the base64 payload, breaking the group-of-4 length on nearly every frame (0 build records decoded before the fix, 625 after). All three fixed same-session; see tools/log_parser/README.md.', 'Tooling', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('fel_infused_weapon_avoidance_at_scale', 'Fel Infused Attack (276075, Fel Infused Weapon\'s proc) avoidance data at far larger scale than any prior sample: 1,823 hits, 0 miss/dodge/parry/full-resist - only 13 REFLECT events (a different mechanic, target-side spell reflection, not a normal avoidance roll). Strongly reinforces the existing "no-ICD per-hit procs do not roll an avoidable hit check" read (primer §1 v6) with real hit-count volume instead of tooltip-absence inference alone. Crit rate 23.86% (435/1823) - notably BELOW both this character\'s melee-table baseline (~45.63%, from Melee/Sword Specialization/Hammer of the Righteous all clustering 44-46%) and typical hybrid-school rates seen elsewhere (~50-53%). Open question, not yet resolved: why Fel Infused Attack crits well below the melee-table baseline despite being a guaranteed per-hit proc - possibly a crit source that does not benefit from the same crit-rating pool as normal attacks/abilities. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 combat log, character Pumprat, Uldaman.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('voidbound_cleave_crit_signal', 'Voidbound Cleave (907280, Warrior-tagged via "uses Cleave modifiers", see class_origin) crit rate 60.65% (501/826) on Pumprat - about 15 points above this character\'s own melee-table baseline (~45.63%, Melee/Sword Specialization/Hammer of the Righteous cluster 44-46%). Also rolls a real avoidance check (8 dodge, 2 parry out of 836 attempts) confirming it is NOT unavoidable like a periodic/summoned effect. Directionally consistent with the existing "hybrid strikes crit on the spell table" pattern (primer §1 v4, established for Holystrike) extending to Shadowstrike as well, given Voidbound Cleave is tooltip-confirmed physical-weapon-damage + Shadowstrike magic-damage hybrid - but NOT yet confirmed against this character\'s own melee/spell crit sheet split (no character-sheet screenshot available), so treat as suggestive, not settled - same caveat already on record for Titanic Mutilate\'s first crit data. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 combat log, character Pumprat, Uldaman.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('voidbound_lightbound_cleave_dbc_formula', 'Voidbound Cleave (907280) and Lightbound Cleave (907300) share BYTE-IDENTICAL raw DBC EffectBasePoints/EffectBonusCoefficient values. Effect[0] (the tooltip\'s "$s1" bonus term, per "does your weapon damage plus $s1"): EffectBasePoints=8->9 (basepoints+1), EffectDieSides=1, EffectBonusCoefficient=1.0 - a full 1:1 AP-scaling coefficient, notably stronger than any other per-hit coefficient logged in this project (typical range 0.05-0.3). Effect[1] (the "your weapon damage" term): EffectBasePoints=64->65, EffectBonusCoefficient=0.0 - read as ~65% weapon damage, no AP/SP scaling. EffectChainTargets=2 matches "two nearest allies" cleave. CONFIDENCE NOTE: the raw Effect type codes (58, 31) were not matched against a verified SPELL_EFFECT enum table - the bonus-vs-weapon-damage split is inferred from which term carries a nonzero EffectBonusCoefficient paired against the tooltip\'s two-clause wording, not from a named enum lookup. Formula: bonus = 9+AP*1.0, weapon_component = weapon_dmg*0.65. Corrects the Paladin build\'s prior "LC flat 62" assumption, which had no DBC or live-tooltip source found this session. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 Pumprat scouting session, dbc-extract.json.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('improved_cleave_true_magnitude', 'Improved Cleave\'s real per-rank magnitude, confirmed via raw DBC across all 3 ranks (basepoints+1 convention): Rank 1 (12329) EffectBasePoints=39->40%, Rank 2 (12950) EffectBasePoints=79->80%, Rank 3 (20496) EffectBasePoints=119->120%. Clean linear +40%/rank. Tooltip: "Increases the bonus damage done by your Cleave ability by $s1%." Applies to the whole Cleave-modifier-bucket family via the class-tag rule (primer §4) - any card whose tooltip states "uses Cleave modifiers" (Lightbound/Voidbound/Spellbound/Flamebound/Frostbound/Stormbound Cleave, base Cleave itself) should inherit this. At 3/3, applied to the AP-scaling bonus term only (voidbound_lightbound_cleave_dbc_formula): bonus becomes (9+AP)*2.2. CONSEQUENCE: build_paladin-hammerdin.md v8 §7 had ranked Improved Cleave dead-last on the chase list assuming a small flat-and-decaying value - corrected to a much higher priority in v9. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 Pumprat scouting session, dbc-extract.json.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('voidbound_cleave_damage_share_and_parse', 'Voidbound Cleave was 47.7% of Pumprat\'s total logged damage in the 2026-08-03 Uldaman log (1,986,118 of 4,165,003 total across all sources, 826 hits, 60.65% crit) - the single dominant damage source by a wide margin (next: Fel Infused Attack 12.9%). Non-crit hits averaged 1,425 (range 833-2,027), crit hits averaged 3,040 (ratio 2.13x, consistent with a standard physical crit multiplier). Fits the (9+AP)*2.2 + weapon_dmg*0.65 formula in shape for a plausible dungeon-tier AP, though Pumprat\'s actual AP/SP was never captured (no character sheet) so this is not an exact numeric confirmation. See builds/shared/scouted_Pumprat_2026-08-03.md for full derivation and open questions.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('paladin_chase_ability_magnitudes_dbc', 'DBC magnitudes resolved for six §8 chase-list abilities (build_paladin-hammerdin.md v10), all via dbc-extract.json spell_dbc_raw + dbc_spellduration: Divine Storm (53385) = 110% weapon damage to multiple enemies + heal-on-hit (EffectBasePoints 109->110); sanity-checked against Elric\'s own Dawn Strike average (812/hit) - at ~723 avg weapon dmg self-buffed, 110% predicts ~795/hit, same order of magnitude. Avenging Wrath (31884) = +20% all damage/healing, 20000ms/20s duration (DurationIndex 18). Guardian of Ancient Kings (277875) = +15% Holy damage (EffectBasePoints[1] 14->15), 12000ms/12s duration (DurationIndex 29), plus resets/discounts Hammer of the Righteous/Divine Storm/Holy Shock cooldowns - the reset effect is not captured by the flat %. Twisted Mind (284448) = flat +60 Spell Power ($PL*1 = player level x1 = 60 at level 60, NOT a percentage), +3% hit (near-worthless per existing hit walkback), healing/absorb reduction magnitude itself hidden behind a second sub-spell (978705) not in this extract; also bar-changing/stance-type, check for conflicts before slotting. Divine Protection (498) = -50% damage taken (EffectBasePoints[1] -51->-50), 12000ms/12s duration (DurationIndex 29), shares a cooldown-exclusion window with Avenging Wrath - defensive only, not a DPS card. Bloodlust (2825) = +30% melee/ranged attack speed + +20% casting speed (EffectBasePoints index2 29->30, index0 19->20), 40000ms/40s duration (DurationIndex 64). Execution Sentence (954817) remains UNRESOLVED even via DBC - all three EffectBasePoints are the -1 "no value" sentinel and EffectTriggerSpell is empty, meaning its real formula is not captured anywhere in this extract (likely hardcoded script logic) - needs a live tooltip, not further DBC digging. IMPORTANT CAVEAT: none of these spells\' actual COOLDOWNS were resolved - this extract has no SpellCooldowns.dbc-equivalent table, only durations. Any "average uptime" DPS estimate built on these numbers is assuming a cooldown value, not measuring one. SOURCE: 2026-08-03 session, dbc-extract.json.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session'),
    ('method_dps_extrapolation_from_talent_stack', 'Reusable method for projecting a DPS ceiling from a chase list: multiply confirmed per-card %-multipliers MULTIPLICATIVELY, not additively (an older Paladin-build estimate summed them to "~40%" - the correct multiplicative stack for the same four cards is +33.5%, not meaningfully different here but diverges more as more cards stack). For an ability-specific formula change (e.g. Improved Cleave\'s AP-scaling bonus term), compute the per-hit delta directly from the DBC coefficients, propagate through the ability\'s own crit ratio and hit-count share from a real parse, then express as a % of TOTAL logged damage - this avoids needing to separate out the ability\'s weapon-damage component, since only the changed term needs isolating. Always log which stats (AP/SP/crit) the projection was computed FROM, since these decay fast as gear changes - the numbers are a snapshot, the method is what is reusable. Applied 2026-08-03 to build_paladin-hammerdin.md §10a (Improved Cleave + four chase talents -> ~48% ceiling from AP 584/self-buffed sheet).', 'Primer', '§5 (v10)'),
    ('pumprat_demon_package_inconclusive', 'Pumprat\'s active spec (5) carries Summon Felguard + Soul Link + Demonic Tactics 5/5 + Demonic Pact 5/5, but the 2026-08-03 Uldaman log does not meaningfully test the demon package: the summoned pet ("Wrathguard" per this server\'s Summon Felguard flavor, not literally named Felguard) landed only 4 melee swings total in the whole log - functionally idle/not the active pull\'s focus. The "Wild Imp"/"Demonic Persistence"/"Firebolt (Wild Imp)" entries in the same log (481+60 hits) belong to a DIFFERENT player, Oxete (via Hand of Gul\'dan, spellId 954611) - confirmed by SPELL_SUMMON source GUID, do not attribute to Pumprat. Demon-package questions remain open pending a log where the pet is actually active/tanking.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-03 session (Pumprat log)'),
    ('pumprat_inspect_unresolved_talent_ids', 'decode_inspect_export.py run against a live inspect (Pumprat, Darkmoon, Wildcard, spec 5) left 3 talent IDs unresolved against spell-export.json; resolved via dbc-extract.json spell_dbc_raw + dbc_talent. #12855 = Cruelty Rank 4 (direct ID hit in spell_dbc_raw - a genuine rank of Cruelty distinct from both ±3 candidates offered, #12856 Cruelty R5 and #12857 Commanding Presence R2; catalog just does not carry this particular rank). #13806 = Close Quarters Combat Rank 4 (same pattern - direct hit, not Close Quarters Combat R5/Mace Specialization R5/Frost Trap). #15259 = Darkness Rank 1, a Priest Shadow-tree talent (TalentTab id 203): not present in spell_dbc_raw itself (outside the extract\'s scoped ID set, no catalog/hidden_refs neighbor within ±3), found instead via dbc_talent.SpellRank array (talent id 462: ranks [15259, 15307, 15308, 0, 0]) - ranks 2/3 (15307, 15308) ARE in spell_dbc_raw as "Darkness Rank 2/3", confirming the name. Ascension\'s Darkness tooltip reads "Increases all damage done by $s2%. Increases your Shadow damage done by $s2%" - broader than vanilla\'s shadow-only version, consistent with primer §1 (v7) "hybrid/dual scaling turns up in unexpected places, check raw tooltips" pattern. Extends method_rank_id_decoding (primer §5 v8): when a rank ID falls outside spell_dbc_raw\'s scope entirely, check dbc_talent\'s SpellRank arrays for the ID before concluding it is unresolvable - sibling ranks already in scope confirm the name without needing a wider DBC re-extract.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-03 session (inspect: Pumprat)'),
    ('winds_of_winter_crit_driver_identified', 'MAJOR REFINEMENT to winds_of_winter_killing_machine_correlation_v2 and to builds/shared/synergy_winds-of-winter.md \xa75\'s open crit-rate gap: scanned 68 public ascensionlogs.gg reports (ids 2-86) for every character running Winds of Winter or Titanic Mutilate (technique: report -> encounters?includeTrash=true -> character_spell_damage?scope=encounter&participantType=friendlies, filtered by spell_name, per primer INDEX_GUIDE v7\'s "find who plays ability X" method), found ~20 distinct characters, then compared talent boards between high-crit and low-crit performers. HIGH performers (Gunju 97.0% crit/1026 hits/1 report; Titanus pooled 99.0-99.5% crit across 5 reports totaling ~2300 hits once his board matured; Kcdq 92.3-100%; Blasted 91.3%; Ek 97.7%) all share flat "increases crit chance with ALL spells and attacks" talents - Malice (14142, 5/5 on Gunju) and/or Conviction (20121, 5/5 on Kcdq) and/or Combat Expertise (31860, 3/3 on Kcdq and Titanus) - STACKED WITH Killing Machine 5/5 (present on every high performer). LOW performers (Tdoctor 16.9-44.3% crit across 2 reports; Evilelf 0%; Altride 31.2%; Coyc 35.3%; Mindtrix 0%) have NONE of Malice/Conviction/Combat Expertise slotted - Tdoctor\'s board is a mismatched Shadow Priest/Elemental Shaman/Druid mix with no Frost-crit support at all despite running the ability. CONSEQUENCE: the wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md v1 hypothesis (Frostbite+Shatter+Fingers of Frost freeze-crit chain) is NOT what any observed high performer actually runs - zero of the ~20 scanned characters slot Frostbite, Shatter, or Fingers of Frost. Retracted as the primary theory (kept as an untested alternative, since it was never ruled OUT, just never observed IN). The evidence-backed answer is simpler: stack universal flat crit% talents (Malice/Conviction/Combat Expertise) on top of Killing Machine, not a freeze-chain proc combo. Separately notable: Gunju\'s primary_stat is confirmed \'duality\' - direct evidence Path of Duality is live and functional for at least one other character on this server, relevant context for build_paladin-hammerdin.md\'s own open "is Duality even active" question (different character, not a direct resolution). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 scouting session, reports 2-86.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('duality_sp_amp_confirmed_reverses_retraction', 'MAJOR REVERSAL of primer path_duality fact / build_paladin-hammerdin.md \xa74\'s "v4: SP amp x1.75 claims RETRACTED - not visible on a live sheet." A clean, controlled test (AscensionCrafterExport addon, 2026-08-04, character Elric, IDENTICAL gear, EMPTY talent/ability spec so no Lunar Guidance or other conversion talent could contaminate the result) compared Path of Strength vs Path of Duality on the same character back-to-back: Spell Power (all schools) 229 -> 434, a clean 1.895x multiplier on itemized Spell Power. Bonus Healing only rose 229->248 (1.08x) - the amp is specifically a damage-Spell-Power multiplier, does NOT apply to healing power. The original v4 retraction was based on a SINGLE SMALL ITEM SWAP on a talent-loaded character (Lunar Guidance present, confounding the Int->SP path) - exactly the kind of contaminated small-magnitude test the primer\'s own method_no_reroll_to_measure/method_sample_size practices warn against. This full-path-switch, empty-spec, same-gear test is clean and the amp is unambiguously present. Also confirmed in the SAME test: Duality\'s Int->melee-crit and Agi->spell-crit conversions are real - melee crit rating +59 with Strength/gear-crit held constant, spell crit rating +8 despite Agility being IDENTICAL (28) in both exports, proving that channel does not exist at all under Path of Strength (Duality-exclusive unlock, not a hidden baseline conversion). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session, AscensionCrafterExport addon, character Elric, Path of Strength vs Path of Duality back-to-back export.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('duality_attack_power_anomaly', 'NEW OPEN QUESTION found alongside duality_sp_amp_confirmed_reverses_retraction: Path of Duality\'s own tooltip claims "AP = highest of Str or Agi" (primer \xa73). Same controlled test (Elric, identical gear, empty spec, Path of Strength vs Duality): Strength dropped 155->121 under Duality (as expected - Path of Strength\'s own flat Str bonus, ~34 at level 60, matches primer\'s documented curve almost exactly) but Agility stayed at 28 in both, so Strength (121) still dwarfs Agility (28) under Duality and a literal reading of the tooltip predicts AP staying close to the Path of Strength value. Instead Attack Power dropped from 290 to 159 (0.548x) and Ranged Attack Power dropped from 183 to 58. This is NOT the same issue as the already-documented 2026-07-28 patch note ("Path of Duality was not increasing your Ranged Attack Power") - that was a not-increasing-enough bug already fixed; this is AP actively being LOWER than the Path of Strength baseline despite Duality\'s formula nominally using the same (higher) stat. Unresolved whether this is a real formula bug, a different conversion rate than 100%, or something else - needs either a patch-note check or a live tooltip on the Path of Duality passive itself. Practical consequence for Winds of Winter / any dual AP+SP build: net effect is still positive overall (SP gain of 1.895x outweighs the AP loss in the quadratic-CP formula, see wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md \xa74), but the AP loss is real and should not be assumed away when gearing. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session, same test as above.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_stack_dbc_pulls', 'Pulled three spells from the already-cached index/dbc-extract.json (from an earlier Pumprat DBC session - no live client needed, just a local JSON lookup), 2026-08-04. (1) Titanic Mutilate hidden sub-spell 271781: raw description resolves cleanly to "115% weapon damage" (both weapons), "damage increased by 20% against bleeding targets" - the has_hidden_formula=1 mystery is fully resolved, no more $271781s2% placeholder. (2) Frostbound Cleave (907340): Effect[0] type=58 EffectBasePoints=8(->9 basepoints+1)/EffectDieSides=1/EffectBonusCoefficient=1.0 (the "$s1" bonus term = 9+AP*1.0), Effect[1] type=31 EffectBasePoints=64(->65)/EffectBonusCoefficient=0.0 (weapon-damage term = weapon_dmg*0.65), EffectChainTargets=2. BYTE-IDENTICAL to Lightbound Cleave/Voidbound Cleave\'s DBC structure (voidbound_lightbound_cleave_dbc_formula) - upgrades frostbound_cleave_identified_for_winds_of_winter_stack\'s formula from a family-pattern PREDICTION to a DBC-CONFIRMED fact. Applying Improved Cleave 3/3 (+120%, already owned): bonus term becomes (9+AP)*2.2, unchanged from the prior prediction. (3) Winds of Winter (274121): 3 effect slots, indices 0/2 have EffectBasePoints=-1 (the DBC "unused" sentinel, same pattern seen on Execution Sentence) so are not the damage effect; index 1 (type=2, plausibly SPELL_EFFECT_SCHOOL_DAMAGE, NOT independently verified against a named SPELL_EFFECT enum table) has EffectBasePoints=1(->2)/EffectDieSides=22(->max 23) for a small base roll ($m2=2 to $M2=23), and EffectPointsPerCombo=33.75 - a DBC field specifically built for "+X per combo point spent" finisher scaling, strongly suggesting this IS the tooltip\'s literal $b2 term: $b2=33.75/CP. At 5 CP this flat term alone is ~168.75, LARGER than the SP dynamic term (138.24 under Path of Intelligence) - the Path-comparison deltas computed earlier in this session (wip \xa74, "+28.7%"/"154.0 vs 100.2") were on an INCOMPLETE formula missing this baseline; full recompute with the flat term included: Strength 269.0, Duality 297.7 (+10.7%), Intelligence 322.8 (+20.0% vs Strength, +8.4% vs Duality) - ranking unchanged (Intelligence still best) but relative gaps are smaller than previously stated. UNRESOLVED: Effect[1] also carries EffectBonusCoefficient=0.214, a THIRD coefficient not mentioned anywhere in the visible tooltip text (which only writes out SPFR*0.0096 and AP*0.00624 explicitly) - could be an additional baseline SP-scaling term the engine applies automatically, or could be inert if this custom-scripted spell overrides standard engine scaling with its explicit text formula. Needs a live tooltip with real computed min/max damage numbers at 1 CP, cross-referenced against known SP, to settle - flagged as the top "hit harder" open item for the next session. Also still unresolved from the original synergy file: whether the SPFR*0.0096 term is genuinely Frost-school-specific SP or reads as general SP on this server (build_index.py\'s regex still does not extract $SPFR* per the existing extractor-gap note, primer v14). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session, local dbc-extract.json lookup.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('titanic_mutilate_115pct_retracted', 'RETRACTS the "115% weapon damage" figure in winds_of_winter_stack_dbc_pulls. That number was read off spell 271781\'s hardcoded description STRING, not the numeric EffectBasePoints field the game engine actually substitutes into 271779\'s "$271781s2%" template. 271781\'s own EffectBasePoints[1]=69 (->70 under the project\'s standard +1 convention, same convention validated on Improved Cleave/Frostbound Cleave/Lightbound Cleave), and its off-hand-trigger sibling 271782 independently computes to the same 69->70. Cross-validated against a real player capture: Gunju\'s scouted live tooltip (index/scouted/scouted_Gunju_2026-08-03.json, entry_id 36503, matches owned spellId 271779 confirmed via Cards.txt) reads verbatim "Instantly attacks with both weapons for 70% weapon damage" - a flat number, no min-max range, matching a non-random EffectDieSides=1 field. CORRECTED VALUE: Titanic Mutilate = 70% weapon damage per hand (both main-hand and off-hand triggers), not 115%. The 115% string is stale/dead flavor text left over in the DBC, not the live value. Practical impact low - Titanic Mutilate\'s magnitude was never load-bearing for the build\'s DPS-share estimates (Winds of Winter dominates at 60%+), but this is the exact "hardcoded description text vs. the numeric field the template actually reads" trap the project\'s own methodology repeatedly warns about, caught this time via independent live-capture cross-check rather than missed. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v8), local dbc-extract.json + scouted_Gunju_2026-08-03.json cross-reference.', 'DBC pull + scouting cross-check', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('ices_spike_weapon_pct_resolved', 'Ices Spike (913312) weapon% resolved via its own effect_json: EffectBasePoints[1]=64 (->65 under the standard +1 convention) on a proper "$s2%" template reference (not a hardcoded string, so not subject to the titanic_mutilate_115pct_retracted trap). Base = 65% weapon damage as Froststrike. Per its own tooltip\'s stated multipliers ("${$m2*1.75}% ... if a dagger is equipped and ${$m2*0.85}% if a two-hander is equipped"), and Titan\'s Grip counting as two-handed for this purpose: 65% x 0.85 = 55.25% weapon damage as Froststrike under this build\'s actual gear (dual 2H, Titan\'s Grip). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v8), local dbc-extract.json lookup.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('titans_grip_physical_penalty_dbc_confirmed', 'Titan\'s Grip\'s "$S3%" tooltip placeholder (spell 46917) DBC-confirmed: EffectBasePoints[2]=-11 (->-10 under the standard +1 convention) on its third effect slot. Physical damage dealt is reduced by exactly -10%. Matches the figure build_paladin-hammerdin.md already carries from a live in-game tooltip on a different character (confirmed_magnitudes table) - independent second method, same number, no surprise, but now confirmed from this build\'s own source data. Closes wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md \xa710 "hit harder" open item 5 (the placeholder mattered more for this build than for the Paladin one, since Frostbound Cleave and Ices Spike both carry real weapon-damage components subject to the tax, not just Winds of Winter\'s stat-pure nuke). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v8), local dbc-extract.json lookup.', 'DBC pull', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('gunju_tooltip_preview_omits_custom_terms', 'Methodology note: Gunju\'s scouted live-tooltip capture of Winds of Winter (index/scouted/scouted_Gunju_2026-08-03.json) shows an IDENTICAL "2-23 damage" range at every one of the 5 combo-point tiers - i.e. the ascensionlogs.gg per-rank tooltip preview does not evaluate the custom $b2*n / $SPFR*n*n / $AP*n*n script terms at all, only the standard $m2/$M2 fields (which DO match the DBC-derived m2=2/M2=23 base roll exactly, so the site data isn\'t wrong, just partial). Consequence: this capture is SILENT on (does not confirm or refute) the still-open winds_of_winter_stack_dbc_pulls question about the 0.214 EffectBonusCoefficient or the 33.75 EffectPointsPerCombo term - it simply never evaluates them for a per-rank preview render. Do not treat an ascensionlogs.gg per-rank ability tooltip as authoritative for any custom-scripted formula term beyond the base DBC fields. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v8).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_live_spellid_is_274132', 'User-confirmed (2026-08-04, direct statement, not inferred): spell ID 274132, NOT 274121, is the Winds of Winter actually cast on Darkmoon realm - source https://db.ascension.gg/?spell=274132. This is NOT a simple rank/instance split as the wip file v2/v7 guessed - 274132\'s School Damage base roll is 32-97, dramatically larger than 274121\'s 2-23 (both independently confirmed on db.ascension.gg, and 274121\'s figure matches the local dbc-extract.json read exactly). 274132 does NOT exist in the locally cached index/dbc-extract.json (checked directly - only 274118 and 274121 present), so winds_of_winter_stack_dbc_pulls\'s EffectPointsPerCombo=33.75 and EffectBonusCoefficient=0.214 readings, both taken from 274121, CANNOT be assumed to carry over to the actual live spell. Cards.txt/spell-export.json still track ownership via 274121 (the catalog/card canonical ID) - this is consistent with the project\'s established pattern of one canonical "card" ID vs. a different live/runtime spell ID (same shape as Titanic Mutilate\'s 271779 wrapper triggering 271781/271782). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), user-supplied db.ascension.gg link + cross-fetch of 274121/274132/271779/913312/907340.', 'User-supplied source (db.ascension.gg)', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_has_own_cooldown_and_mana_cost', 'MAJOR new mechanical finding, not previously known from any prior source (not in dbc-extract.json, not in Gunju\'s scouted tooltip capture): Winds of Winter (274132) has its own 5-SECOND COOLDOWN, independent of the GCD (GCD listed separately as 1s) and independent of combo points spent. It also costs "25% of base mana" per cast, NOT Energy - confirmed via db.ascension.gg. This means Winds of Winter cannot be cast more than once per 5 seconds no matter how fast combo points are generated, and the finisher runs on an entirely different resource pool (Mana) than its own combo-point generators. Cross-referencing the rest of the ability stack on the same site reveals the WHOLE kit runs on three separate resource pools, one per class each ability borrows modifiers from: Titanic Mutilate (borrows Mutilate/Rogue) = 50 Energy, Ices Spike (borrows Hemorrhage/Rogue) = 35 Energy, Winds of Winter (borrows Cone of Cold/Mage) = 25% base Mana + 5s CD, Frostbound Cleave (borrows Cleave/Warrior) = 20 Rage, no cooldown, 0 GCD. This is a new instance of the class-tag rule (primer §4) extending beyond damage modifiers into RESOURCE TYPE - not previously documented anywhere in this project. CONSEQUENCE: the existing energy_sustain_stack_for_winds_of_winter talent picks (Vitality/Focused Attacks/Relentless Strikes/Combat Potency/Natural Energy/Slaughter from the Shadows) remain valid for Titanic Mutilate + Ices Spike specifically, but do nothing for Winds of Winter\'s Mana cost or Frostbound Cleave\'s Rage cost - both are unaddressed gaps as of this session. Also cross-validates Ices Spike (65% weapon dmg) and Frostbound Cleave (9 flat/65% weapon dmg) exactly against the prior session\'s local DBC reads. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), user-supplied db.ascension.gg link, cross-fetch of spells 274132/271779/913312/907340.', 'User-supplied source (db.ascension.gg)', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_demon_package_not_the_discriminator', 'Checked the Demon Package (synergy_portable-multiplier-packages.md: Demonic Tactics/Demonic Pact/Master Demonologist/Demonic Knowledge) against the 5 locally-scouted Winds of Winter characters (index/scouted/*.json). Result: 4/4 HIGH performers run at least one member - Titanus (Demonic Pact 5/5 + Demonic Tactics 5/5), Blasted (Master Demonologist 5/5 + Demonic Pact 5/5 + Demonic Knowledge 3/3 - the deepest investment seen), Kcdq (Demonic Tactics 5/5), Gunju (Master Demonologist 3/5 + Demonic Tactics 3/5, partial ranks). BUT the one LOW performer checked, Tdoctor (16.9-44.3% crit), ALSO runs Demonic Tactics 5/5 - so the package is NOT what discriminates high from low Winds of Winter performance (that remains Malice/Conviction/Combat Expertise + Killing Machine, per winds_of_winter_crit_driver_identified). Consistent with the original synergy_portable-multiplier-packages.md framing: this is a broadly-popular, cross-class-portable pick most "Hero" classless characters take regardless of their core engine, not a Winds-of-Winter-specific synergy. Still worth adding to our own build though - see winds_of_winter_demon_package_unconditional_split. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), cross-referencing already-scouted JSON files (no new API calls).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_demon_package_unconditional_split', 'Pulled full per-rank tooltip text for all 4 Demon Package talents from 3 scouted characters (Blasted/Gunju/Titanus). Two of the four have a SELF-buff clause that is UNCONDITIONAL - no active pet/demon required at all: Demonic Tactics ("Increases critical strike chance for YOU, your tamed pet, and your Wild Imps by X%" - the "you" clause is not gated) and Demonic Pact ("Increases your spell damage done by X%" is a separate, unconditional sentence from the raid-buff clause that DOES require a Summoned - not Enslaved - demon\'s crits). At max rank (5/5 each): +10% crit (any table, matches its own "critical strike chance" wording, no school restriction) and +10% flat spell damage done, both with zero pet management required. The other two ARE fully pet-conditional: Master Demonologist\'s entire effect (both the self and pet portions) requires "that demon is active" - Gunju\'s partial 3/5 investment is likely WASTED since his scouted build carries no demon-summon ability on the bar at all; Demonic Knowledge explicitly reads "your active demon\'s Stamina plus Intellect" - fully dead without a pet out. Master Demonologist\'s payoff varies sharply by pet type: Felguard/Enslaved Demons give "+X% ALL damage done, -X% damage taken" (school-agnostic, would buff Winds of Winter); Imp only buffs Fire; Succubus only buffs Shadow - neither relevant to a Frost build. CONFIRMED OWNED at or near max rank in Elric\'s own Cards.txt: Demonic Tactics (30248, talentNormal 5/5), Demonic Pact (47240, talentNormal 5/5), Master Demonologist (23825, talentNormal 5/5), Demonic Knowledge (35693, talentNormal+Golden 3/3) - zero reroll chase needed for any of them. RECOMMENDATION for wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md (not yet applied to the recommended board pending user direction, per 2026-08-04 session "hold for a core" instruction): Demonic Tactics 5/5 + Demonic Pact 5/5 are pure free upside, no rotation cost - Master Demonologist/Demonic Knowledge would require committing to actual Felguard/Enslaved-demon pet upkeep, a real design decision not yet made for this build. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_ice_floes_may_reduce_own_cooldown', 'HIGH-VALUE LEAD, directly relevant to the just-discovered Winds of Winter 5s hard cooldown (winds_of_winter_has_own_cooldown_and_mana_cost): Ice Floes (55094, owned talentNormal+Golden 3/3, confirmed via Cards.txt) reads at 3/3 "Reduces the cooldown of your Frost Nova, Cone of Cold, Ice Block and Icy Veins spells by 33%." It names Cone of Cold VERBATIM - satisfying the primer §5 "named lists outrank generic wording, no proc-test needed" rule already used elsewhere in this doc for Improved Cone of Cold\'s damage amp. Winds of Winter is class-tag-confirmed to borrow Cone of Cold modifiers (primer §4 class-tag rule). If Ice Floes\' cooldown-reduction clause follows the same borrowed-modifier pathway as Improved Cone of Cold\'s damage clause already does, it would cut Winds of Winter\'s newly-discovered 5s cooldown to ~3.35s - directly bearing on the open "does Energy regen or the cooldown bind cast frequency" question (wip \xa710 hit-often item 2). NOT YET PROC-TESTED - this is a prediction under the class-tag rule, same confidence tier as any other borrowed-modifier inference, not a confirmed fact. Found while scanning scouted characters\' talent boards for Frost-relevant picks (Kcdq/Blasted/Gunju all run Ice Floes 3/3) in response to the user\'s Demon-package/Shadow-Frost-synergy question. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_no_shadow_synergy_found', 'Directly answers user question (2026-08-04): none of the 4 checked Winds of Winter HIGH performers (Gunju/Titanus/Kcdq/Blasted) run any Shadow-school-specific damage talent. Their Frost/multi-school picks: Ice Floes 3/3 (all 3, Cone of Cold CD -33%, see winds_of_winter_ice_floes_may_reduce_own_cooldown), Concussion 5/5 (Kcdq - "Increases your Frost, Fire, and Nature damage done by 5%", owned by Elric per Cards.txt id 16108 talentNormal+Golden 5/5, NOT currently in wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md\'s tracked Frost-dmg% list which only has Piercing Ice/Arctic Winds/Black Ice/Improved Cone of Cold - a 5th one to add), Tundra Stalker 5/5 (Kcdq - "+15% dmg to targets with your Frost Fever" - CONDITIONAL on a Frost Fever debuff source this kit does not currently have, likely dead as-is), Elemental Weapons 3/3 (Blasted/Titanus - buffs Windfury/Flametongue/Frostbrand/Earthliving WEAPON IMBUES specifically - conditional on running one of those exact imbues, none currently planned, primer\'s weapon-imbue-exclusivity rule applies). By contrast, the ONE low performer checked (Tdoctor, Shadow Priest) is saturated with Shadow talents (Shadow Power, Misery, Twisted Faith, Pain and Suffering, Improved Shadowform, Shadow Embrace, Backdraft, Vampire Lord) and NONE of them touch Frost at all - reinforces the existing wip-file conclusion that his board is a mismatched, non-synergistic pile rather than evidence Shadow investment helps. CONCLUSION: no Shadow synergy exists or is worth chasing for this Frost-school build; the real untapped Frost lead from this scan is Concussion (owned, free, currently untracked) and the Ice Floes cooldown question above. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('glacial_spike_unlocks_tundra_stalker', 'MAJOR NEW FIND: Glacial Spike (284177, owned abilityNormal 1/1, seen on Gunju\'s bar) - real tooltip: "Summons a Glacial Spike, dealing ${$m1+($SP*0.129)+($AP*0.0838)} Frost damage, slows enemies by $S2% for $d and infects targets with Frost Fever. This uses Cone of Cold modifiers. Damage is split when hitting more than 3 enemies." Two consequences for wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md: (1) it is itself a real, linear (not quadratic) SP+AP-scaling Frost nuke that borrows Cone of Cold modifiers - same class-tag family as Winds of Winter, so it benefits from Improved Cone of Cold (45%, owned) and Spell Impact (see spell_impact_verbatim_cone_of_cold_amp) the same way. (2) it APPLIES FROST FEVER, which is the missing enabler for Tundra Stalker (50130, owned 5/5, previously flagged likely-dead in winds_of_winter_no_shadow_synergy_found because this kit had no stated Frost Fever source) - Tundra Stalker\'s own wording ("your SPELLS AND ABILITIES deal 15% more damage to targets infected with your Frost Fever") is GLOBAL, not restricted to the Cone of Cold family, so if Glacial Spike keeps Frost Fever applied it would buff Winds of Winter, Ices Spike, Frostbound Cleave, and Titanic Mutilate simultaneously. Tradeoff: this is a genuinely new button, in tension with the build\'s stated minimal-button design goal - not yet decided whether to add it. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), scanning scouted Gunju/Titanus/Kcdq/Blasted/Tdoctor JSON for Frost/Cold/Cone of Cold keyword hits per user request.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('spell_impact_verbatim_cone_of_cold_amp', 'Spell Impact (12469, owned talentNormal 3/3) verbatim-names Cone of Cold in its tooltip: "Increases the damage of your Arcane Explosion, Arcane Blast, Arcane Barrage, Arcane Orb, Blast Wave, Fire Blast, Scorch, Pyroblast, Ice Lance and Cone of Cold spells by $s1%." Satisfies the primer §5 "named lists outrank generic wording, no proc-test needed" rule - same tier of confidence as Improved Cone of Cold\'s existing 45% amp. Gunju runs it at 2/3 with a resolved live value of 6% (implies 3%/rank, so Elric\'s already-owned 3/3 = 9%). A real, previously-untracked damage amplifier for Winds of Winter (and Glacial Spike, if added - see glacial_spike_unlocks_tundra_stalker). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), scouted Gunju talent board.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('elemental_focus_mana_sustain_lead', 'Elemental Focus (16164, owned talentNormal 1/1, seen on Titanus\'s board) is the strongest Mana-sustain lead found so far for Winds of Winter\'s newly-discovered 25% base Mana cost (winds_of_winter_has_own_cooldown_and_mana_cost): "After landing a critical strike with a Fire, Frost, or Nature damage spell or ability, you have a $h% chance to enter a Clearcasting state. The Clearcasting state reduces the resource cost of your next $16246n Magic spells or abilities by $16246S1%." Given the ~99-100% Frost crit rates already measured on these same high-performer characters (winds_of_winter_crit_driver_identified), this proc would fire close to every Winds of Winter cast if it triggers off Frost crits specifically (tooltip says "Fire, Frost, or Nature" - Winds of Winter qualifies). Exact proc chance ($h%), reduction magnitude ($16246S1%), and how many spells it covers ($16246n) are all still templated/unresolved even in this live-captured tooltip - same site-rendering gap noted elsewhere (gunju_tooltip_preview_omits_custom_terms) for a different set of variables. Directionally promising, not yet quantified. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), scouted Titanus talent board.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('seal_fate_extra_combo_point_lead', 'Seal Fate (14193, owned talentNormal 3/3, seen on Blasted\'s board at 1/3) found while scanning for Frost/Cold keywords (matched on its capstone mentioning "Cold Blood", not a Frost-damage hit - flagged here since it is separately relevant to the still-open 5th-combo-point-source question, wip \xa75/\xa710). Tooltip: "Your critical strikes from ROGUE ABILITIES THAT ADD COMBO POINTS have a $h% chance to add an additional combo point." Titanic Mutilate is Rogue-tagged (borrows Mutilate modifiers, class-tag rule) and adds combo points (2/cast) - Seal Fate\'s crit clause should apply to it directly, giving a chance at a 3rd CP from a single Titanic Mutilate cast. The secondary clause ("Increases damage done by Eviscerate, Rupture, Deadly Throw and Crimson Tempest by 10%") does not help - none of those abilities are in this kit. Not proc-tested. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), scouted Blasted talent board.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('arctic_reach_radius_only_not_damage', 'Arctic Reach (16758, owned talentNormal 2/2, seen on Gunju\'s board) verbatim-names Cone of Cold but is a RANGE/RADIUS talent, not a damage amp: "Increases the range of your damaging spells by X yards and the radius of your Frost Nova and Cone of Cold spells by 20%." Widens Winds of Winter\'s cone width for AoE/trash coverage, does not increase single-target damage. Carries a "does not stack with other similar effects" exclusivity clause - unchecked what else is in that bucket, flag before ever slotting alongside another range/radius talent. Lower priority than the damage amps found in the same scan (spell_impact_verbatim_cone_of_cold_amp, glacial_spike_unlocks_tundra_stalker). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), scouted Gunju talent board.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('frost_fever_synergy_not_actually_combined_by_anyone', 'HONEST NEGATIVE RESULT, checked per user request (2026-08-04): the Glacial Spike -> Frost Fever -> Tundra Stalker combo (glacial_spike_unlocks_tundra_stalker) is mechanically sound per both spells\' raw tooltips, and matches synergy_portable-multiplier-packages.md\'s pre-existing "Package 2: DK Disease Multiplier Package" (Tundra Stalker/Rage of Rivendare + Icy Touch/Plague Strike, flagged there as "Not yet tested on our own build"). But checking all 5 locally-scouted Winds of Winter characters (Gunju/Titanus/Kcdq/Blasted/Tdoctor) for BOTH halves of the combo shows NOBODY has assembled it: Gunju owns Glacial Spike 1/1 (the Frost Fever SOURCE) but has no Tundra Stalker and no other disease-amplifying talent at all; Kcdq owns Tundra Stalker 5/5 (the AMPLIFIER) but has no Frost Fever source whatsoever (no Icy Touch, no Glacial Spike, no Plague Strike/Rage of Rivendare) - meaning Kcdq\'s own Tundra Stalker investment is very likely dead weight, same failure mode predicted for our own build before Glacial Spike was found. Titanus/Blasted/Tdoctor have neither half. CONSEQUENCE: this is a real, tooltip-grounded synergy prediction under the class-tag/named-effect rules, NOT an empirically-validated "top players do this" pattern - do not represent it as observed-in-the-wild. Treat with the same confidence tier as any other unproven class-tag prediction until tested on our own character. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9), cross-referencing all 5 scouted JSON files for Tundra Stalker/Rage of Rivendare/Icy Touch/Plague Strike/Glacial Spike presence.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('seal_fate_weak_adoption', 'Checked Seal Fate (seal_fate_extra_combo_point_lead) adoption across all 5 scouted Winds of Winter characters per user request: only 1/5 (Blasted) runs it, and only at a partial 1/3 rank. Gunju, Titanus, Kcdq, Tdoctor do not run it at all. This is NOT a broadly-adopted "top players do this" pattern the way the Demon Package or Ice Floes/Improved Cone of Cold are (those showed 3-4/5 or higher). The underlying mechanic (crits from Rogue CP-adding abilities have a chance for a bonus CP, should apply to Titanic Mutilate via the class-tag rule) remains sound and worth testing, but should be weighted as a low-confidence/untested lead, not a validated pattern, when building the candidate pool. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session (v9).', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('energy_sustain_stack_for_winds_of_winter', 'Recommended Energy-sustain talent stack for wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md, 2026-08-04, all six ALREADY OWNED (no reroll chase): Vitality 3/3 (flat Energy regen%, unconditional), Focused Attacks 3/3 ("melee auto attacks, offensive spells and abilities have a chance to give energy" - generic wording, covers every ability in the kit), Relentless Strikes 3/3 ("finishing moves have a % chance PER COMBO POINT to restore energy" - Winds of Winter is explicitly tagged a Finishing move in its own tooltip, rolls 5x per cast since the build always dumps at 5 CP), Combat Potency 3/3 (off-hand melee attacks chance to generate Energy - relevant once Titan\'s Grip is slotted and off-hand is swinging), Natural Energy 1/1 ("Your Mutilate critical strikes restore energy" - names Mutilate verbatim, applies to Titanic Mutilate via class-tag/named-list rule), Slaughter from the Shadows 3/3 ("Reduces the energy cost of...your Hemorrhage" - names Hemorrhage verbatim, Ices Spike borrows Hemorrhage modifiers so this should reduce ITS cost directly). CAVEAT: Malice\'s own capstone also has an Energy clause ("gain Energy when your Garrote, Rupture, or Crimson Tempest deal damage") but NONE of those three abilities are in this kit - Malice earns its slot for the crit% alone, its Energy clause is dead here, do not double-count it as sustain. NOT owned, optional chase: Glyph of Mutilate (flat Energy cost reduction on Mutilate, likely applies to Titanic Mutilate via the same class-tag pattern) - a nice-to-have, not essential given the six owned picks above. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('honor_among_thieves_shared_by_both_reference_players', 'Both Gunju and Titanus (the two strongest Winds of Winter performers found, primer/seed_confirmed winds_of_winter_crit_driver_identified) run Honor Among Thieves 3/3 (51701, owned, talentNormal) - a genuine passive combo-point generator: "When anyone in your group critically hits with a damage or healing spell or ability, you have a $s1% chance to gain a combo point. Cannot occur more than once every 3 seconds." Exact proc chance unresolved ($s1% placeholder in export) - needs live tooltip/DBC pull. Requires a group (inert solo), chance-gated with a 3s ICD, so cannot be the sole 5th-combo-point source but reduces reliance on an active filler (Ices Spike, wip \xa75) in group content. Distinguished from other shared talents that are Energy-sustain, not CP generation: Combat Potency (off-hand crit -> Energy), Vitality (+Energy regen%), Natural Energy (owned, 1/1: "Your Mutilate critical strikes restore energy" - names Mutilate verbatim, likely applies to Titanic Mutilate via the borrows_from/class-tag relationship and the "named beats generic" rule, primer \xa75). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session, cross-referencing previously-scouted Gunju/Titanus talent boards against spell-export tooltips.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('frostbound_cleave_identified_for_winds_of_winter_stack', 'Frostbound Cleave (907340, Froststrike school, "uses Cleave modifiers" -> Warrior-tagged per class_origin, same "-bound Cleave" family as Lightbound Cleave/Voidbound Cleave) identified as a strong low-button addition to the wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md kit, 2026-08-04. Owned (abilityNormal). Hybrid Froststrike double-dips Frost dmg% modifiers on its magic half (primer hybrid_school_rule) - benefits from the SAME Piercing Ice/Arctic Winds/Black Ice stack already planned for Winds of Winter, zero extra talent cost. Same family as Lightbound Cleave, which build_paladin-hammerdin.md \xa711 documents as "queued off-GCD at all times" - does not compete for rotation slots/button presses. Improved Cleave (20496, the R3/max-rank spellID specifically per method_rank_id_decoding\'s distinct-spellID-per-rank pattern) is ALREADY OWNED (talentNormal) - ready to slot with no reroll chase, applying its DBC-confirmed +120% multiplier (improved_cleave_true_magnitude fact) to Frostbound Cleave\'s AP-scaling bonus term via the shared Cleave-modifier bucket. PREDICTED (not independently DBC-verified for this specific spell, extended by family pattern from voidbound_lightbound_cleave_dbc_formula): weapon_dmg*0.65 + (9+AP)*2.2 at Improved Cleave 3/3. Using the three Path snapshots from intelligence_path_beats_duality_for_winds_of_winter: predicted hit 973 (Strength, AP 290), 700 (Duality, AP 159), 606 (Intelligence, AP 101) - the one place the Path of Intelligence recommendation costs real damage, since this ability is AP-scaling and Intelligence sacrifices AP hardest. Does not change the Path recommendation (Winds of Winter is 60%+ of total damage and still wins under Intelligence) but is a real, quantified tradeoff worth weighing once a parse is run. Recommended stack: Titanic Mutilate x2 (4 CP) + Ices Spike (5th CP, also Froststrike hybrid, same Frost-dmg% synergy) + Winds of Winter @ 5CP (spender) + Frostbound Cleave (off-GCD weave, does not touch the combo-point economy at all). SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('intelligence_path_beats_duality_for_winds_of_winter', 'Third data point completing the 3-way Path comparison (Elric, identical gear, empty spec, same test as duality_sp_amp_confirmed_reverses_retraction): Path of Intelligence measured at Spell Power 576 (2.515x the Path of Strength baseline of 229 - NOT a clean 2x despite the primer\'s "SP DOUBLED" paraphrase, 118 higher than a literal doubling predicts, same "measured ratio does not match the documented paraphrase" pattern as Duality\'s 1.895x vs its old "1.75x" folklore figure - both real effects, neither tooltip wording is exactly right, live tooltip screenshots would resolve the exact numbers). Attack Power 101 (0.348x, lower than Duality\'s 0.548x - expected, Intelligence has no AP-conversion clause at all). Melee/ranged crit stayed at the Path of Strength baseline (15.70%, zero bonus) vs Duality\'s +4.22%. Two clean confirmations of ALREADY-DOCUMENTED primer facts: Intellect rose +79 (180->259) and Spirit rose +40 (37->77), matching primer path_intelligence\'s existing "~79 @ 60" / "~40" flat-grant figures almost exactly - validates the export tool\'s accuracy. SURPRISING RESULT: plugging all three paths into the actual Winds of Winter formula at 5 CP (SP*0.0096*n^2 + AP*0.00624*n^2) gives Strength 100.2, Duality 129.0, Intelligence 154.0 - Intelligence scores HIGHEST despite its much lower AP, because SP\'s coefficient dominates the formula enough that Intelligence\'s SP lead (576 vs 434) outweighs its AP deficit (101 vs 159). Cross-checked against Seal of Command\'s judge formula (0.19*weapon+0.08*AP+0.13*SPH), same ordering: Strength 145.1, Duality 165.7, Intelligence 189.3. Also notable: main-hand weapon damage average INCREASED across paths despite AP dropping (485.2 -> 508.2 -> 559.6) - weapon damage on this server is not simply AP-derived, so Titanic Mutilate (pure weapon-%, no AP/SP coefficient in its own tooltip) does not lose value under Intelligence the way a naive AP-only read would predict. CONSEQUENCE for wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md: challenges that file\'s "Path: Duality, the only real candidate" framing - Intelligence beats Duality on both formulas checked so far; Duality\'s one remaining edge is melee/ranged crit (relevant to Titanic Mutilate\'s own crit chance and autos). Sheet-math on 3 static snapshots, not a real parse - primer\'s own stated gold standard (a dummy parse under each candidate path) would confirm this outright and is the natural next test. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 session, AscensionCrafterExport addon, character Elric, third of three back-to-back path exports.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('elric_gear_already_sp_itemized', 'CORRECTS an over-generalization in wip_winds-of-winter-frostblade.md v2\'s gear section. build_paladin-hammerdin.md \xa74/\xa76 states "neither weapon itemises SP or Int" - TRUE and reconfirmed for the weapons specifically (The Light\'s Hope: 0 Spell Power, exact match) via a live in-game export (custom addon index/AscensionCrafterExport/, 2026-08-04), but the wip file had over-generalized this to "the whole kit needs re-gearing toward SP" without checking the rest of the armor. Real per-slot data shows 12 of Elric\'s 13 non-weapon armor/jewelry pieces carry Spell Power directly, totaling 229 - within 8 points of Gunju\'s (the reference Winds of Winter build) 237 gear Spell Power total. Elric\'s gear also carries 162 Crit Rating vs Gunju\'s 51 (3x). The one real, confirmed gap is Attack Power: Gunju\'s dual weapons + trinket carry 156 flat AP, Elric\'s gear carries 0 (Elric\'s 290 total AP comes entirely from Strength conversion, not itemization). Revised gearing plan: chase AP-itemized weapons/trinkets specifically, not a full re-gear. SOURCE: 2026-08-04, AscensionCrafterExport addon output, character Elric.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
    ('winds_of_winter_crit_rate_time_series', 'Titanus\'s own Winds of Winter crit rate was NOT consistently high - it improved sharply over a ~5-day window as his board matured, pooled per report (character_spell_damage, hits/crits): report 26 (2026-07-25, "Tonx MS leveling") 18 hits/2 crits = 11.1%; report 32 (2026-07-26, "ms") 256 hits/88 crits = 34.4%; report 47 (2026-07-30, "illegal damage") 299 hits/299 crits = 100.0%; report 69 (2026-07-31) 455/452 = 99.3%; report 68 (2026-08-01) 589/583 = 99.0%; reports 74/75 (2026-08-02) 431/428 = 99.3% and 615/612 = 99.5%. The jump from 34.4% (07-26, n=256, not a small-sample fluke) to 100.0% (07-30, n=299) in a 4-day window is the clearest single piece of evidence that the crit rate is talent/gear-driven and acquirable, not an inherent property of the ability or a fixed passive rate - consistent with winds_of_winter_crit_driver_identified\'s Malice/Conviction/Combat Expertise+Killing Machine theory (those are exactly the kind of talents a leveling/gearing character picks up over days, not instantly). Damage share climbed alongside it: 14.7% -> 22.7% -> 23.0% -> 42.8% -> 41.3% -> 38.4% -> 40.5%. SOURCE: 2026-08-04 scouting session, reports 26/32/47/68/69/74/75.', 'Scouting', '2026-08-04 session'),
